From 9d31a2c5f8b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] backends: probe POSIX shm API before building backend

Some Android NDK/Bionic targets do not expose the POSIX shm_open/shm_unlink
API required by QEMU's hostmem-shm backend. Do not rely on host_machine.system()
to identify Android: QEMU's cross configuration can report the build OS for
this probe. Check the actual target compiler headers instead.

The Android app uses ordinary file-backed virtual disks and does not require
this optional host backend. Keep it enabled on other hosts that provide the
API.

---
 backends/meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/backends/meson.build b/backends/meson.build
index 0000000000..1111111111 100644
--- a/backends/meson.build
+++ b/backends/meson.build
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ system_ss.add([files(
   'confidential-guest-support.c',
 ), numa])
 
-if host_os != 'windows'
+if host_os != 'windows' and cc.has_function('shm_open', prefix: '#include <sys/mman.h>')
   system_ss.add(files('rng-random.c'))
   system_ss.add(files('hostmem-file.c'))
   system_ss.add([files('hostmem-shm.c'), rt])
--
2.43.0
